1
00:00:02,377 --> 00:00:05,797
[PLAYING RED HOT CH ILI PEPPERS'
"UNDER THE BRIDGE"]

2
00:00:07,757 --> 00:00:11,177
[SINGING]
And I don't ever wanna feel

3
00:00:11,344 --> 00:00:12,974
Like I did that day

4
00:00:13,430 --> 00:00:16,850
Take me to the place I love

5
00:00:17,017 --> 00:00:18,897
Take me all the way

6
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:22,730
[SINGING IN FALSETTO]
And I don't ever wanna feel

7
00:00:22,897 --> 00:00:24,607
Like I did that day

8
00:00:24,774 --> 00:00:26,444
Take me to the place I love...

9
00:00:26,609 --> 00:00:27,649
[SQUEALS]

10
00:00:27,819 --> 00:00:28,859
[MUSIC STOPS]

11
00:00:29,529 --> 00:00:31,359
(Penny:)Fellas, please.

12
00:00:31,531 --> 00:00:35,371
(Howard:)Penny, come on.
We were just finding our sound.

13
00:00:35,910 --> 00:00:40,370
(Penny:)You found it. It's the sound of a cat
being run over by a lawn mower.

14
00:00:42,125 --> 00:00:43,755
Well, I'm really very busy.

15
00:00:43,918 --> 00:00:47,208
Is there any way we can put this off
until I have more time to prepare?

16
00:00:47,964 --> 00:00:51,054
(Leonard(entering on the phone):)Of course,
but, uh, you understand my trepidation.

17
00:00:51,217 --> 00:00:52,797
- What's that about?
- Not a clue.

18
00:00:52,969 --> 00:00:55,429
(Leonard:)Can't we just postpone it till the spring?

19
00:00:55,597 --> 00:00:57,137
(Leonard:)Maybe next summer?

20
00:00:57,307 --> 00:00:59,057
(Sheldon:)This should be fairly easy to deduce.

21
00:00:59,225 --> 00:01:02,475
(Sheldon:)He's holding the phone to his left ear.
Ears do not cross hemispheres.

